cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "monolog: fused, GPU-resident fixpoint evaluation for recursive graph queries"
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite the paper below."
type: software
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: "https://github.com/arsho/monolog"
abstract: >-
  monolog runs a recursive Datalog round as a single fused CUDA kernel over a
  persistent, device-resident data structure instead of a chain of separate
  relational-algebra operators. One atomic write performs deduplication, novelty
  detection, and union at once, removing intermediate materialization,
  relation-wide sorting and merging, and per-round temporary allocation. Because
  the fixpoint state and the change count stay on the device, the whole loop can
  be replayed as a CUDA graph or executed from a single launch with a conditional
  CUDA graph node. This repository is the single-GPU artifact for the paper: four
  execution strategies for each of transitive closure, same generation, and
  weakly connected components, plus the datasets, scripts, environment, and
  frozen results used to compare against the MNMGDatalog and GPUlog engines.
keywords:
  - GPU
  - recursive queries
  - transitive closure
  - connected components
  - CUDA graphs
  - kernel fusion
  - incremental evaluation
